<title>FINLAND: Markka, Finnish bond report.</title>
<headline>Markka, Finnish bond report.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds ticked slightly lower with German Bunds after the Bank of England raised its minimum lending rate by 25 bps to 6.00 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>The markka was stable without fresh incentives after a brief knee-jerk jump with the dollar on the rate hike.</p>
<p>&quot;Bonds will follow Germany while waiting for the U.S. data,&quot; a bond dealer said.</p>
<p>Money rates remained volatile after Tuesday's unrest and came off earlier lows after the Bank of England's move, dealers said. But they said trade was less nervous than on Tuesday. @</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
